			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Consolidate protocol architecture documentation\n\nThe architecture documentation has been restructured to reflect the current\ngRPC protocol layer. `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` now presents a\nsingle `Vine.proto` schema with `MountainService` and `CocoonService`,\nreplacing the prior split between `Vine.proto` and `Spine.proto`.\n\nService definition tables, port allocation, and configuration sections are\nupdated to show the finalized topology: Mountain Vine on 50051, Cocoon Vine\non 50052, and Air Vine on 50053. Multiplexed streaming channels are documented\nin the service tables.\n\n`Documentation/GitHub/DeepDive.md` is revised to match: the architecture diagram\nnow includes `AirClient`, the key modules table reflects the current source tree\nstructure, and integration points include a dedicated listening addresses table.\n\nThese changes align documentation with the live implementation and remove\nreferences to the deprecated Spine coordination layer.",
			"SHA": "2af32ec226ad75062ba84ce96b0f38dd155183e5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-29T13:55:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				110,
				4
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Normalize table column widths across architecture documentation\n\nAligned the column widths in the Protocol Files table (Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md) and Integration Points table (Documentation/GitHub/DeepDive.md) to improve visual consistency and readability in rendered Markdown.\n\nThe changes adjust the dash separators in the table header rows to create uniform column spacing, removing asymmetry in the pivot table render. A minor text wrapping fix was also applied to DeepDive.md introduction and a line break was consolidated in README.md.\n\nAdditionally, removed the now-unused commit_message.json file from the Vine root directory.\n\nThese are documentation refinements with no functional impact, ensuring the Architecture.md and DeepDive.md guides render cleanly in GitHub's Markdown viewer.",
			"SHA": "bf80b653a9d0c47d6aff6c6dd56c85abaa080a61"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T19:33:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				111,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Vine): Remove inner flow detail and planned Grove node from architecture diagram\n\nThe Mermaid graph in README.md has been simplified to match the current production topology. The internal crates of Mountain (multiplexer, client.rs, generated bindings) were removed from the diagram as they are implementation details, not architectural boundaries. The planned Grove WASM host node and its transport layer were also removed, as Grove is not part of the active protocol stack.\n\nThe bidirectional gRPC link now correctly connects VineServer directly to GRPCClient, reflecting the live Mountain ↔ Cocoon communication path.",
			"SHA": "5b8fa8bf5ca3285c6f5482b0228f30e23d7b6eff"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T19:10:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				111,
				3
			],
			"Message": "docs(Project): Remove Grove references from Vine architecture documentation\n\nThe Grove WASM extension host component was removed from the active protocol layer. This update removes dead references to `Grove.proto`, the Grove gRPC client, and the `NetworkGrovePort` configuration from the Vine architecture documentation across `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md`, `Documentation/GitHub/DeepDive.md`, and the root `README.md`.\n\nThe gRPC topology is now streamlined to Mountain ↔ Cocoon (Vine/Spine prototypes) and Mountain ↔ Air (Air.proto). The documentation diagrams, tables, and port listings are updated to reflect the current production stack.",
			"SHA": "f7e1043f334b29028a153f2e1570b7d908e3fa88"
		}
	],
